      - 2 frames form the training pair (s1.s, s1.d): their non-zero interior color-sets are identical.
      - 1 frame is the test sprite (s2): its non-zero interior colors are DIFFERENT from the training pair's.
  training_pair_rule:
    kind: one of {endpoints, fill, sym_fill, comp_checker, invert0, sym (rotation/reflection)}; pair must be related by exactly one such transform
    palette: pair interiors use 1-2 non-background colors drawn from {1,2,3,4,5,6,8} (not equal to frame color or bg colors)
    pixel_count: each pair interior has 3-32 non-zero pixels; s1.s and s1.d pixel counts may differ (e.g. endpoints/fill)
  test_sprite (s2):
